  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `crates/tools/src/holder_library_weldon.rs` (new): `picker_rows()` groups each taper's Weldon bores into one row (\"BT30 Weldon\", \"BT40 Weldon\", \"CAT40 Weldon\", \"TTS Weldon\"); `resolve(name, shank_d)` / `weldon_for(taper, shank_d)` turn a grouped pick into the library's existing per-bore entry whose bore takes the tool's shank. A shank no standard bore takes is refused with the existing `LibraryError::Shank` text (\"a Ø7.000 mm shank does not fit - the holder takes a BT30 Weldon bore: Ø6.000, ...\").\n- The library data is unchanged: one entry per bore, so the outline, body diameter, fit check and collision bands of a grouped pick are exactly the old entry's.\n- `SetToolBody::library` (`library_body`) and `AddTool::with_holder` resolve through `resolve`, so the GUI, `set_tool_holder` and `add_tool`'s `holder` key all take \"BT40 Weldon\"; `AddTool` records the resolved name (\"BT40 Weldon 10 mm\"). MCP schema text says so.\n- UI: the holder picker lists the grouped rows; the note under a Weldon pick names the resolved bore and body for the stored tool's shank, or the refusal.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/2018-weldon-per-taper.md` (done ahead of #2016: the grouped pick resolves to a concrete entry at command time, which #2016's reference can store later).\n\n## How tested\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: tools, app and ui suites green (macOS); `cargo clippy -p camcraft-tools -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\n\nPinning tests:\n- `holder_library::weldon::tests::the_picker_shows_one_weldon_row_for_each_taper`\n- `holder_library::weldon::tests::a_10mm_shank_gets_the_10mm_bore_and_its_body` (10 mm bore, 35 mm body)\n- `holder_library::weldon::tests::a_shank_with_no_standard_bore_is_refused_by_name` (pins the message)\n- `holder_library::weldon::tests::a_picked_weldon_draws_the_old_entrys_collision_bands` (every bore of every taper, band for band)\n- `crates/app/tests/holder_library.rs::a_weldon_pick_takes_the_bore_of_the_tools_shank` (command lands the old entry's outline, judged holder and bands; refusal by name through the command)\n- `egui_app::tests::tool_holder::one_weldon_row_for_each_taper_takes_the_bore_of_the_shank` and the updated `the_picker_lists_the_tts_holders_and_names_the_collar`\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Machine `.mch` `tooling.default_holder` still takes only a per-bore name (a grouped default would need the tool's shank at mount-rule time); unchanged.\n- `list_holder_library` still lists the per-bore data entries (the data is unchanged).\n- No pixel snapshots touched; no Windows run.\n\nFork synced at upstream/main 31f8d03d7 (branched from upstream main per the session brief).\n\nChangelog: The holder picker shows one Weldon entry for each taper; the bore and body come from the tool's shank, and a shank with no standard bore is refused by name.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #2018\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
